/ Stage 1 (decision 867): text's face without the name floor. `source.cs:115` today reads
/ `_type.kind.IsText || _type.Name is "text"` — the Name fallback is only there because
/ a kind built inline from a name (`type/this.cs:149`) answers `IsText=false` even for a
/ text's own kind. When the type is born whole, the registered md kind carries
/ `Text = true` (its mime `text/markdown` begins with `text/`), so `kind.istext` alone
/ answers; the Name floor can go. Red on runtime2: today the fresh `kind.@this("md")`
/ has `_text = false`, so `%x!type.kind.istext%` reads false (expected true).
TextKindIsText
- set %x% = "a" as text/md
- assert %x!type.kind.name% equals "md"
- assert %x!type.kind.istext% equals true
